{
 "id": "2023-song-scenic",
 "name": "Scenic Beauty of a Painted Retaining Wall (SBE)",
 "description": "Faithful replication: same task, scale and photographs as the paper (the authors' 20 photographs of the giant retaining wall in Heye Village, Jiuzhaigou, figshare doi:10.6084/m9.figshare.21700970, CC BY 4.0). Scenic Beauty Estimation of an engineering structure: after a short background text about the wall and its murals of natural scenery and Tibetan folk culture, participants rate each photograph on five indicators (color richness, visual effect, cultural connotation, vegetation coverage, overall coordination) from −3 (very poor) to +3 (very good), stored 1–7 as in the authors' data. Gender, education and professional background (landscape-related or not) come first. The paper standardises each evaluator's ratings into an SBE value per photo and regresses SBE on the five indicators; it finds that murals with depth and visual extension, folk-culture content and good coordination raise scenic beauty. The page source holds the paper's SBE value and indicator means for every photo. Differences from the original study: (1) the background text is a short summary written from the paper, as the original text is not published; (2) photos are shown in random order; (3) the photos are cut from the authors' published grid, about 620 px wide; (4) English instead of Chinese. Cite: Song, Zhou, Xiao, Zeng, Wu & Song (2023), PLOS ONE 18(6): e0287251.",
 "author": "Song et al.",
